drafts.raw:
Can Spring be far behind when Winter’s stormy hand is shown?  
When I fire my fate, it thunders from this laślaż— the night’s raw blaze, I call it war, and here I raise / My promise by a rogue leaf called laska;  

Która z rzemionek w tym zwinn

Beware, as I declare my name anew—fearless, bold at every turn, so let not silence break within this storm;

Fearless, my heart will stand unyielding, and in the night's dark hush I vow our courage can not be eclipsed.

Wait—must end on same word it began with:

plays.verse:
A soul, my dear, will arrive at last;
I wait for you beneath the dark gate—
Until the hour when we meet, witaj.

